# bank1.map — annotations for bank1.s
#
# Labels sourced from original_source/src/*.ROU and *.MUS
# Applied by: annotate raw/bank1.s info/bank1.map src/bank1.s
#
# Note: PDS !labels are global scope. ca65 @labels are cheap locals
# scoped between global labels. Since many bank1 branches cross
# global label boundaries, we use prefixed global names (e.g. adsr_loop)
# instead of @locals to avoid scope errors.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECTION banners
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

SECTION  bank1_entry       MUSIC1.MUS
SECTION  trytoentername    HISCORE.ROU
SECTION  titlescreen       TITLE.ROU
SECTION  fx_setup          SOUNDFX.ROU
SECTION  restupdatecoin    NEWBITS.ROU
SECTION  robinhearts       EXPLODE.ROU
SECTION  printrobin        PRTROBIN.ROU

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Structure comments
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

INLINE  860F  --- music data: note frequency tables, instruments, song data ---
INLINE  9CC4  --- hiscore screen data: initnames + message strings ---
INLINE  A1D6  --- pulsetable (16 bytes) + FX_TABLE pointers + FX bytecodes ---
INLINE  A838  --- sprite/shape data table (144 bytes) ---
INLINE  A930  --- message data: game over, completed, treasure, lives info ---
INLINE  ABD9  --- secrettable: 24 secret area modification records ---
INLINE  AF40  --- sincostable: 64-entry sine/cosine lookup (0-64 range) ---
INLINE  AF81  --- exploderoubitsl/h: explosion routine dispatch tables ---
INLINE  AF8F  --- flashrobin: invincibility flash timing (6 bytes) ---
INLINE  B165  --- CHR tile pattern data + padding ---

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transferred comments from alpha source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# MUSIC1.MUS
INLINE  8007  Start music: A = tune number (1-9). Sets up 4 voice macro pointers then triggers
INLINE  803A  Trigger: clears all music vars, sets IRQ, calls NEW_MACRO x4
INLINE  8066  Play music: called once per frame to advance the music driver
INLINE  80A1  Delay bit: increments delay counter, triggers DO_VOICES when tempo reached
INLINE  80B5  ADSR: processes attack/decay/sustain envelopes for all 4 channels
INLINE  8391  Do wobble check: handles vibrato phase cycling and amplitude ramping
INLINE  83CD  Sub voice: lower pitch of voice X by A (adds to period = lower frequency)
INLINE  83F0  Add voice: raise pitch of voice X by A (subtracts from period = higher frequency)
INLINE  8417  New macro: advance macro pointer to next pattern for voice X. If ch0 reaches end, loops or stops
INLINE  84A2  Do voices: process note data for all 4 voices, decode pattern bytes into notes and instruments

# HISCORE.ROU
INLINE  9818  Try to enter name: strips leading zeros, inserts commas, runs hiscore table check
INLINE  9857  Display high scores: calls tryhiscore, sets up screen, starts tune 3
INLINE  9874  Looking at high scores: main loop - vblank, name entry or pulse, start button check
INLINE  9899  Setup high scores: loads chr tiles, prints hiscore screen layout, sets fade colours
INLINE  98E6  Enter name: D-pad scrolls through letters (rate-limited to every 8 frames)
INLINE  990C  Choose letter: A button confirms selection. If letter=0, acts as start. Max 8 chars
INLINE  9940  Delete letter: B button deletes last entered letter
INLINE  9985  Flash letter: positions sprite cursor at name entry position, pulses colours
INLINE  9C71  Copy high scores to RAM: validates saved data integrity, copies defaults if corrupt

# TITLE.ROU
INLINE  9D8A  Title screen: alternates between title graphics and high score display
INLINE  9DAA  Show title: sets up title screen graphics
INLINE  9DB0  Wait for start: main title loop - vblank, sprites/music, timeout and start key
INLINE  9DEA  Put on title sprites: swaps pattern table, pulses colour, places logo sprites
INLINE  9E1B  Setup title screen: loads chr blocks, prints title message, configures sprites
INLINE  A1B3  Pulse colour: oscillates palette entry X through pulsetable based on frame counter

# SOUNDFX.ROU
INLINE  A433  FX envelopes: handles attack envelope - increments volume until max reached
INLINE  A454  FX try decay: handles decay envelope - decrements volume until min reached
INLINE  A47E  FX setup: A = effect number. Checks priority, sets channel with attack/decay/volume/pitch
INLINE  A52A  FX play: once per frame - outputs volume/pulse to APU, advances envelopes and instructions
INLINE  A571  FX next: reads next FX instruction triplet (command, data, cycles) from stream
INLINE  A5CD  FX do: 1=raise pitch, 2=lower, 3=set note, 5=raise slow, 6=lower slow, 7=trigger sub-FX
INLINE  A68C  FX real speed: fractional speed divider for smooth pitch slides

# NEWBITS.ROU
INLINE  A6DA  Rest/update coin: handles on-screen treasure/heart display, sparkle, and pickup collision
INLINE  A7C3  Pulsing heart: renders heart items with pulsing animation
INLINE  A7E8  Put in heart bank: finds coin/treasure entry in coinco table matching map position
INLINE  A8C8  Start float up number: stores coin position and starts 64-frame float-up counter
INLINE  A8EE  Float up number: animates collected treasure value floating upward
INLINE  AAE2  Print 6 treasures: draws treasure type icons on info screen with sparkle effects
INLINE  AB12  Add sparkle to treasures: randomly spawns sparkle animations using PRNG seed
INLINE  AB6C  Redefine water: animates water tile patterns by cycling CHR data (maps 0-4 only)

# EXPLODE.ROU
INLINE  AD12  Robin hearts: sets up heart particle position relative to Robin's XY (-18 Y, -4 X)
INLINE  AD2D  Update hearts: iterates 3 heart particle groups, dispatches via jump table
INLINE  AE21  Get value: sine/cosine lookup with 8-bit multiply by size for circular positioning
INLINE  AE62  Put spin heart: writes one heart sprite entry to sprite block buffer
INLINE  AE79  Print circle of hearts: renders 4 hearts in rotating circle using sin/cos offsets

# PRTROBIN.ROU
INLINE  AF95  Print Robin: main sprite rendering - invincibility flash, direction, animation dispatch
INLINE  AFC5  Print Robin 1: renders legs based on anim frame, handles crouching offsets
INLINE  B033  Work out body: selects from 8 running frames or standing/shooting poses
INLINE  B058  Work out head: renders head, then falls through to print legs
INLINE  B09D  Work out head routine: calculates head Y, randomly blinks/looks around every 32 frames
INLINE  B0D6  Print Robin on ladder: alternates leg frames based on Y position, handles facing
INLINE  B137  Print Robin shooting: selects shooting body frame based on firing timer
INLINE  B159  Subtract height of sprite: adds sprite height offset for stacking parts vertically

